From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Chulo <cchulo.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus-ally: report the ROG Xbox Ally X20 top-right key
 (0xa0) as KEY_PROG2

The ROG Xbox Ally X20 (board RC74XA) has a button at the top right of
the screen that sends vendor code 0xa0 on the N-KEY interface: "5a a0"
on press, "5a 00" on release. No earlier Ally sends 0xa0, and neither
ally_x_raw_event() nor the Ally config input path in ally_raw_event()
knows it, so the button does nothing.

Report it as KEY_PROG2, one plain key, on the Ally X gamepad input
device and on the "ASUS ROG Ally Config" input device. KEY_PROG2 is not
used by any other Ally button: 0xa6 (the left button, Armoury Crate on
the X20) reports KEY_F16 or BTN_MODE, 0x38/0x93 report KEY_PROG1 or the
Steam Quick Access chord, 0xa7/0xa8 report KEY_F17/KEY_F18.

0xa0 gets KEY_PROG2 whatever qam_mode is set to. The driver emits no
Steam chord for it. InputPlumber, which SteamOS uses for this
controller, sets qam_mode=0 and maps keys to Steam actions through its
capability maps. It needs a key that is distinct from 0xa6. A first
version of this patch reported KEY_F16 for 0xa0 (the 0xa6 key), so both
top buttons did the same thing under InputPlumber, and with qam_mode=1
it synthesised BTN_MODE+BTN_A. That chord raced with InputPlumber's own
mapping.

The ally-x20-steamos InputPlumber capability map turns KEY_PROG2 into
Steam's screenshot action, matching the red capture label the owner
reports on that button. Other users can map it to anything.

hid-asus is not changed. Its asus_input_mapping() table maps vendor
usage 0xa6 to KEY_F16, but with CONFIG_HID_ASUS_ALLY reachable
hid-asus skips the Ally endpoints 0x83, 0x87 and 0x04 (asus_probe() in
hid-asus.c returns -ENODEV for them), and the 0x5a vendor reports are
delivered to hid-asus-ally. The other hid-asus devices (ROG laptop
keyboards) may use 0xa0 for something else, so a hid-asus-wide mapping
would be wrong too.

No device-table change is needed. The X20's N-KEY device enumerates as
0b05:1b4c (hidraw node 0003:0B05:1B4C.*), the same ID as the ROG Ally X
(USB_DEVICE_ID_ASUSTEK_ROG_NKEY_ALLY_X), so it already binds to this
driver.

Derived from:
- ovenham/rog-ally-x20-steamos-speaker-qam-fix (README button table
  and tools/x20-buttons.sh: Armoury Crate at the top left sends 0xa6,
  the right-side button sends 0xa0 on press and 0x00 on release; N-KEY
  device 0b05:1b4c),
  https://github.com/ovenham/rog-ally-x20-steamos-speaker-qam-fix
- hhd-dev/hhd src/hhd/device/rog_ally/base.py (AllyHidraw.produce():
  0xa6 is the left button, 0x38/0x93/0xa0 the right button)
- drivers/hid/hid-asus.c in the same tree (0xa6 -> KEY_F16 "ROG Ally
  QAM button"; Ally endpoints skipped when CONFIG_HID_ASUS_ALLY is
  reachable)

Base: linux-integration 7.2.7-valve2 plus the previous patches in this
series. Applies without them as well.

TODO(hw): on an RC74XA confirm with hidraw that the top-right button
sends 5a a0 and nothing else, and that the evdev node of "ASUS ROG Ally X
Gamepad" shows exactly one KEY_PROG2 press and release per press.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
index 224aa9c..cd45ebc 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
@@ -36,6 +36,15 @@
 #define ROG_ALLY_X_MIN_MCU 313
 #define ROG_ALLY_MIN_MCU 319
 
+/*
+ * Vendor key code in byte 1 of 0x5a input reports on the N-KEY interface.
+ * The ROG Xbox Ally X20 (RC74XA) sends 0xa0 for the button at the top
+ * right of the screen. No earlier Ally sends it. The driver reports it
+ * as KEY_PROG2, a key no other Ally button uses, and leaves its meaning
+ * to userspace.
+ */
+#define ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT 0xa0
+
 #define FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID1 0x5d
 #define FEATURE_KBD_LED_REPORT_ID2 0x5e
 
@@ -1483,6 +1492,7 @@ static struct ally_gamepad_cfg *ally_gamepad_cfg_create(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	input_dev->uniq = hdev->uniq;
 	input_dev->name = "ASUS ROG Ally Config";
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, KEY_PROG1);
+	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, KEY_PROG2);
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, KEY_F16);
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, KEY_F17);
 	input_set_capability(input_dev, EV_KEY, KEY_F18);
@@ -1591,6 +1601,8 @@ static int ally_x_raw_event(struct ally_x_device *ally_x, struct hid_report *rep
 			input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_F16, data[1] == 0xA6);
 			input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG1, data[1] == 0x38 || data[1] == 0x93);
 		}
+		/* X20 top-right key: one plain key in both qam modes, no chord */
+		input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_PROG2, data[1] == ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT);
 		/* QAM long press */
 		input_report_key(ally_x->input, KEY_F17, data[1] == 0xA7);
 		/* QAM long press released */
@@ -1720,6 +1732,7 @@ static struct input_dev *ally_x_setup_input(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, BTN_THUMBR);
 
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, KEY_PROG1);
+	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, KEY_PROG2);
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, KEY_F16);
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, KEY_F17);
 	input_set_capability(input, EV_KEY, KEY_F18);
@@ -2632,6 +2645,7 @@ static int ally_raw_event(struct hid_device *hdev, struct hid_report *report, u8
 
 	if (cfg && !ally_x) {
 		input_report_key(cfg->input, KEY_PROG1, data[1] == 0x38);
+		input_report_key(cfg->input, KEY_PROG2, data[1] == ALLY_X20_KEY_RIGHT);
 		input_report_key(cfg->input, KEY_F16, data[1] == 0xA6);
 		input_report_key(cfg->input, KEY_F17, data[1] == 0xA7);
 		input_report_key(cfg->input, KEY_F18, data[1] == 0xA8);
